/* book: lead: Castigliano's theorem turns a strain energy formula into a deflection. Write the strain energy U of a linear elastic body as a function of an applied load P, differentiate with respect to P, and the result is the displacement Δ at that load, along that load. It is the quickest route to the deflection of a beam, a frame or a truss once the strain energy is written down. */
