/* book Worked example 2: Q: A stepped steel bar has E = 200 GPa and pull P = 50 kN. Segment 1: 0.4 m, 400 mm²; segment 2: 0.6 m, 200 mm². Find the extension.
   1. Each segment carries the full pull, so U = P²L₁/(2A₁E) + P²L₂/(2A₂E).
   2. L₁/(A₁E) = 0.4/(400 × 10⁻⁶ × 200 × 10⁹) = 5.0 × 10⁻⁹ m/N; L₂/(A₂E) = 0.6/(200 × 10⁻⁶ × 200 × 10⁹) = 1.5 × 10⁻⁸ m/N; sum 2.0 × 10⁻⁸ m/N.
   3. U = ½ × 2.0 × 10⁻⁸ × P² = 1.0 × 10⁻⁸ P² J; at P = 50 000 N, U = 25 J.
   4. Δ = ∂U/∂P = 2.0 × 10⁻⁸ P m = 2.0 × 10⁻⁸ × 50 000 = 1.0 × 10⁻³ m = 1.0 mm. The thin segment gives 0.75 mm of it.
   Answer: Extension 1.0 mm; stored energy 25 J. */
